  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced capacities of African member States to provide credible labour statistics and improve data dissemination strategies in Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO in Africa is focused on improving labour statistics to track progress on SDG decent work-related indicators. Key areas include data collection, identifying needs for new statistics, and producing analytical publications. The 2016 resolution on Advancing Social Justice and the SDG indicators framework emphasize the importance of evidence-based research. The ILO&apos;s strategy, guided by the Abidjan Declaration, aims to enhance data for Africa&apos;s priorities, such as youth employment, gender equality, and economic development. The ILO will continue to build regional capacity for labour market statistics and research, supporting the SDG framework. This involves regular data collection, training with lasting impacts, and effective dissemination systems. The goal is to ensure high-quality, timely research and statistics to advance the Decent Work Agenda and monitor progress towards the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development. The ILO will build on 2018-2019 efforts to enhance labour migration statistics and strengthen capacity in Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
